==Battleground==
*1 [[Brollow]] spawns as the boss.
*1 [[Brollow]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Brollow]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is mandatory to start the stage by immediately summoning a 75¢ meatshield, not too slow if possible (e.g. [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]), as the Brollows here have '''760,000 HP''' and deal '''600,000 damage''' even on 1-crown and will pretty much nuke most units in two hits. Fortunately, their long backswing and low range makes them easy to stall and pick off with DPS units, or exploit their range disadvantage and abuse [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] so they'll barely even move. Once they're gone, the stage is won from this point.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] - While the Brollows are too much to tank, Metal Macho only takes 1 damage from all sources and has 12 health at level 20. This allows Metal Macho to shrug off their attacks for quite a while at a fairly low cost, although other meatshields should be brought along to compensate for his downtime.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - With Massive Damage to Floating, Fishman provides a fair bit of extra DPS to the Brollows, and has enough range to avoid their attacks (215>150).
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] - While not strictly necessary, Sanzo can be helpful here with Area Attacks that have a 20% chance to Slow [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating enemies]] for 4 seconds. Being able to outrange Brollows as well, Sanzo can create an impenetrable line of defense by removing Brollow's speed advantage.
*[[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] - Easily able to permafreeze the brollows, especially if you use the [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] [[Cat Combo]]. Be wary of his Single Attack.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] - If you can get him to keep hitting the Brollows on their backswing, Headmaster Cat Jobs can use his weaken effect to completely shut down any pushing power the Brollows have, by making them deal damage even frailer [[Cat Units]] can survive easily.
*[[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - With 4 meatshields and Sanzo Cat, he can comfortably knockback the Brollows to death. If you have his Explosions talent maxed out, this becomes even easier.

==Trivia==
*Throne of Phone's Japanese name, Terehō Daiza (テレホー台座, "Telepho Pedestal"), is a pun on テレホーダイ ''terehōdai'' (off-peak telephone call price reduction) and 台座 ''daiza'' (pedestal). テレホーダイ is also the name of a [[wikipedia:ja:テレホーダイ|telephone service]] from 1995.

